            "description": "The modern geographic association for the unnamed Roman aqueduct structure.⁠ Mina is a town located near the aqueduct.",
            "details": "<p><span> The cartographic placement relies on the </span><span>Atlas Archéologique de l'Algérie</span><span> (AAA) and the Barrington Atlas framework. As the specific Latin identifier for this localized water infrastructure is absent from the primary textual record, the feature is designated by its proximity to the modern geographic location of Mina to resolve the spatial placeholder and facilitate analysis of provincial engineering networks.</span></p>\r\n<p><span> </span></p>",
            "end": 1999,
